PREDECESSOR BLOCK (why IOS/MAC build+test are BLOCKED — evidence)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This artifact "Depends on: P4 core". P4 core has NOT wired the new shared-surfaces source group
into the Xcode build in this slot, and the allowed-files scope for this prompt is ONLY
apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/KpiOverviewCard.* + this log (project.yml and .swiftlint.yml
are out of scope; Honesty Covenant #7 forbids bypassing the predecessor by editing them).

Reproducible evidence (xcodegen generate; Xcode 26.5):
  * project.yml app targets source `TeslaSync/feature-views` + `TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets` but
    NOT `TeslaSync/shared-surfaces`. Generated TeslaSync.xcodeproj => 0 references to
    "shared-surfaces" => KpiOverviewCard.* is absent from every target (app, test, macOS).
  * The per-surface test convention (e.g. feature-views/AiUsageCard.Tests.swift, 224 *.Tests.swift)
    is emitted as a build file in the APP target's Sources phase, while the XCTest bundles source
    only `Tests/Unit`. So per-surface `*.Tests.swift` (incl. mine) are not routed into a test
    target by the current project.yml — another P4-core wiring responsibility.
Net: the gate's full-app `build test` cannot faithfully exercise THIS surface until P4 core adds the
shared-surfaces source group (+ a test-target route) to project.yml/.swiftlint.yml. The surface
itself is complete and independently proven correct (steps [1]-[5]); the block is the predecessor
wiring, not platform capability (the KMP xcframework builds) and not a defect in this surface.

